think Second lap this run. The README next-rungs line (after the double-line box corpus landed) names arrows and the diagonal box marks. Arrows are the crux: where the box corpora frame and rule, arrows point -- the mark a terminal (Dexter/Scooter) uses to scroll a list or mark a selection.
think Chose a tight, contiguous, low-risk set: the six basic arrows U+2190..U+2195 (left, up, right, down, and the two axis double-heads). Left the eight diagonals for their own round rather than risk sloppy hand-drawn diagonals on a 5x7 grid.
think Design: shaft on the middle row/column with a filled-triangle head for the four cardinals (mirror/flip of one drawing), outward chevron heads for the two double-heads. The drawings are the specification; coverage lifted from the art.
obs Followed the exact box-corpus pattern (explicit ascending codepoint table, art-is-spec, round-trip + present + distinct + legible-band). Ink came out 9..12 of 35 as designed; set an honest band 6..16. Compression reported as a fact (encoded 252 > raw 210) -- like the sparse box marks the round-length stream carries per-run overhead, so the round-trip is the proof, never a false compression-direction invariant.
loom witness=font5x7_arrow_witness marks=6 cell=5x7 ink_lo=9 ink_hi=12 encoded_bytes=252 raw_bytes=210
